No, they don't eat. So you're supposed to get on, and never
get off.

The fastest thing you can saddle is a unicorn or warhorse. But
those have little HP.

Perhaps the strongest thing is a dragon, which gives you flying
but they are slow. (walk only about as fast as you do. I
forgot whether they were slower...)

Checkout the riding spoiler:
http://groups.google.com/group/rec.games.roguelike.nethack/browse_frm/thread/e07dff0278ed3fbd/b9278e2fb1aaf64a

Of those creatures, warhorses and unicorns are often far too
weak, dragons are too slow, centaurs are weak...

Ki-Rin on the other hand, look awesome in comparison. I haven't
tried Jabberwock myself, but I do know that warhorses and
unicorns are just too hard to keep alive unless you have
extra healing and a stethoscope. Even then, they tend
to charge at enemies at 10 HP and die in a single hit...

Centaurs however, should be able to eat wraith corpses.
Ki-Rin can quaff !oGain Level and become tougher (in
my wizmode test, it went upto lvl 49 with 280 HP.) In
pure power, Dragons are probably better, but they are
just... so slow. Dragons can eat wraith corpses, but
not !oGain level.

